---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../../../components/Hero.astro';
import LangSwitch from '../../../../components/LangSwitch.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of use of the Pétanque Game app | Ludiven Studio"
	description="General terms of use and sale of the Pétanque Game mobile game: account, virtual coins, purchases, online play and fair play, liability, governing law."
	lang="en"
	alternates={{ fr: '/jeux/petanque/cgu/', en: '/en/jeux/petanque/cgu/', es: '/es/jeux/petanque/cgu/', de: '/de/jeux/petanque/cgu/', it: '/it/jeux/petanque/cgu/' }}
>
	<div class="wrapper stack gap-12 legal">
		<div class="stack gap-8">
			<LangSwitch
				lang="en"
				links={[
					{ lang: 'fr', href: '/jeux/petanque/cgu/' },
					{ lang: 'es', href: '/es/jeux/petanque/cgu/' },
					{ lang: 'de', href: '/de/jeux/petanque/cgu/' },
					{ lang: 'it', href: '/it/jeux/petanque/cgu/' },
				]}
			/>
			<Hero
				title="Terms of use — Pétanque Game"
				tagline="Coins for the game, and fair play online."
			/>
		</div>

		<p class="updated">
			<strong>Pétanque Game</strong> app (<code>com.ludivenstudio.petanquegame</code>) — last updated:
			27 October 2026.
		</p>
		<p class="updated">
			This is a courtesy translation. In case of discrepancy, the
			<a href="/jeux/petanque/cgu/" hreflang="fr">original French version</a> prevails.
		</p>

		<div class="summary">
			<p><strong>Key points before you play:</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li>The game is <strong>free</strong>, with ads if you accept them. Coin packs and the "No ads" option can be bought, but everything can be earned by playing.</li>
				<li>The game's coins and items <strong>have no cash value</strong>: they cannot be traded, resold or refunded, except where the law requires it.</li>
				<li>Purchases go through <strong>Google Play or the App Store</strong>. Coins you buy go to your game account and disappear if you delete it.</li>
				<li>Online: <strong>no cheating, no offensive names</strong>. A reported name can be removed, and an account that cheats can be suspended.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>1. Purpose and acceptance</h2>
			<p>
				These terms govern the use of the Pétanque Game mobile game (hereinafter "the Game") and the sale of
				its paid content. By installing or using the Game, you accept them. If you refuse them, do not use the
				Game and uninstall it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>2. Publisher</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Company name: <strong>Ludiven Studio</strong></li>
				<li>Legal form: EURL (French single-member limited company) with share capital of 1&nbsp;000&nbsp;€</li>
				<li>Registration: 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586 R.C.S. Vienne — SIRET 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586&nbsp;00013</li>
				<li>EU VAT number: FR20&nbsp;999253586</li>
				<li>Registered office: 1166 route de la Ranche, 38440 Châtonnay, France</li>
				<li>Publication director: Ludiven Studio</li>
				<li>Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a></li>
			</ul>
			<p>See also the <a href="/mentions-legales/">legal notice</a> (in French).</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>3. The Game</h2>
			<p>
				Pétanque Game is a 3D pétanque game, in games to 13 points: against the computer, with two players on
				one phone, or online against another player (with a friend through a code, or in a quick match), in
				singles, doubles or triples. It also offers leagues, an online ranking, daily challenges and a shop of
				boules, jacks, throwing circles, scenery and outfits.
			</p>
			<p>
				Playing against the computer and with two players on one phone works without an account and offline.
				Coins, the shop, leagues, online play and purchases need the internet and an account. Connection and
				equipment costs are borne by you.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>4. Account</h2>
			<p>
				You sign in with your <strong>Google</strong> (Android) or <strong>Apple</strong> (iPhone) account.
				The Game is meant for <strong>adults</strong>: it is not intended for under-18s.
			</p>
			<p>
				You are responsible for what is done from your account. Keep access to your Google or Apple account:
				it is what lets you get your progress back. A game account cannot be transferred or sold.
			</p>
			<p>
				You can delete your account at any time: Options › "Delete my account". Deletion is final: a deleted
				account, its coins and its items cannot be given back. What is erased is described in the
				<a href="/en/jeux/petanque/confidentialite/#suppression">privacy policy</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>5. Coins and virtual items</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>Coins</strong> are earned by playing (games against the computer, daily bonus, challenges,
				leagues, optional videos) or bought in packs (see §6). They are used to buy items in the Game (boules,
				jacks, throwing circles, scenery, outfits) and to enter league cups.
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Coins and items are a <strong>personal user licence</strong> within the Game. You do not own them.</li>
				<li>They <strong>have no cash value</strong>: they cannot be converted into money, traded between players, resold or refunded, except where the law requires it.</li>
				<li><strong>Leagues</strong> are skill cups against the computer: the entry fee and the winnings are in coins, never in money.</li>
				<li>They are tied to your game account and <strong>disappear if you delete it</strong>.</li>
				<li>The publisher may change the coin prices, the winnings and the catalogue. An item you already have stays yours. Coins or items obtained through an error in the Game, through cheating or through a refunded purchase may be taken away.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>6. Purchases</h2>
			<p>The Game sells, for real money:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>coin packs</strong>, credited to the game account signed in at the time of purchase;</li>
				<li>the <strong>"No ads"</strong> option, a one-off, permanent purchase, with no subscription, which removes the ads between games. The optional videos that give coins are still offered.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				The price is the one shown in the Game at the time of purchase, in your currency, including taxes. A
				price change has no effect on purchases already made.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Payment goes exclusively through Google Play or the App Store</strong>, depending on your
				phone, and follows their terms. The publisher has no access to any banking data. The proof of purchase
				is issued by the store. Parental controls on purchases are those of the store.
			</p>
			<p>
				"No ads" is tied to your Google Play or App Store account: after a reinstall, Options › "Restore
				purchases" gives it back. If a purchase is not credited, write to us with the store's proof of
				purchase.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>7. Right of withdrawal and refunds</h2>
			<p>
				Coins and the "No ads" option are digital content supplied immediately after purchase. In accordance
				with Article L221-28 13° of the French Consumer Code, by requesting their immediate supply, you
				<strong>waive your right of withdrawal</strong> of fourteen days, which you acknowledge at the time of
				purchase.
			</p>
			<p>
				Refunds are handled by the store where the purchase was made:
				<a href="https://support.apple.com/en-gb/HT204084" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple</a> or
				<a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Play</a>.
				We cannot refund in their place, but we can help you with the process: write to us. Your statutory
				guarantees of conformity remain in force.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>8. Advertising</h2>
			<p>
				The Game shows ads provided by the ad networks ironSource Ads and Unity Ads (Unity Technologies),
				through Unity LevelPlay, only if you accepted them in the "Ads and privacy" window or in Options › "Ad
				choices". If you decline them, you play as usual, with no ads and without the videos that earn coins.
				These networks choose the ads: the publisher does not control their
				content and is not liable for the products or services they present. Your consent and the data used
				are described in the
				<a href="/en/jeux/petanque/confidentialite/">privacy policy</a> (§6).
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>9. Online play: the rules</h2>
			<p>Online, you agree to play fair:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>no cheating</strong>: do not modify the Game, its files or its network exchanges, do not use automated tools, do not use a flaw in the Game to win coins, games or ranking points;</li>
				<li>a <strong>decent name</strong>: nothing offensive, hateful, discriminatory, sexual or promotional, not another person's name, and no surname, number or address. The Game's filter refuses the most common offensive names, but it does not catch everything;</li>
				<li>do not disrupt other players' games, or the service.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				A ranked game left before the end counts as lost, even if the Game was closed. To report a name or a
				player, write to <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>
				and give the name.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>10. Moderation and penalties</h2>
			<p>
				The publisher may, without notice, <strong>remove or replace a name</strong> that breaks these rules,
				<strong>erase or correct a rating</strong> in the ranking, take away coins and items obtained by
				cheating, and <strong>suspend or delete an account</strong> for a serious or repeated breach. To
				challenge a decision, write to
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>11. Intellectual property</h2>
			<p>
				The Game, its code, its 3D models, its images, its sounds and its texts belong to Ludiven Studio or its
				licensors and are protected by intellectual property law. You receive a personal, non-exclusive right
				of use. Components by other authors and their licences are listed in the Game (Options › "Credits and
				licenses") and in the <a href="/mentions-legales/">legal notice</a>. "Pétanque" is a generic term: the
				Game is not affiliated with any federation.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>12. Changes, interruption and discontinuation of the service</h2>
			<p>
				The publisher may change the Game, add or remove features, and adjust the coin prices, the winnings
				and how often ads are shown. The online features rely on Unity's services: they may be interrupted for
				maintenance or by an outage.
			</p>
			<p>
				The publisher may stop all or part of the service, in particular if running it is no longer viable or
				if a store requires its removal. It will then tell players in the Game, with reasonable notice. Playing
				against the computer will remain possible as long as the installed version works on your phone.
				Discontinuation does not give rise to a refund of coins or items, except where the law requires it.
			</p>
			<p>
				These terms may change. The date of the update appears at the top of the page. In the event of a
				significant change, the Game will let you know; continuing to play means you accept them.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>13. Liability</h2>
			<p>
				The Game is provided as is. The publisher does not guarantee that it works without interruption or
				error on all phones, nor that the online services are always available.
			</p>
			<p>
				The publisher can only be held liable in the event of proven fault, and its liability is limited to
				direct and foreseeable damage. It does not cover a dispute between players, nor progress lost through
				the deletion of the account or the loss of access to the Google or Apple account. Nothing here excludes
				its liability in the event of gross negligence or physical injury, nor limits your mandatory consumer
				rights.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>14. Personal data</h2>
			<p>
				The processing of your data is described in the
				<a href="/en/jeux/petanque/confidentialite/">Pétanque Game privacy policy</a>, which forms part of these
				terms.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>15. Governing law and disputes</h2>
			<p>
				These terms are governed by <strong>French law</strong>. If you are a consumer living in another member
				state of the European Union, you keep the mandatory protections of your country.
			</p>
			{/* TODO legal: replace with the mediator's name, address and website once adhesion is signed (art. L612-1). */}
			<p>
				If there is a problem, write to us first: we will look for an amicable solution. If there is no
				solution within one month, you can turn to a consumer mediator free of charge (Article L612-1 of the
				French Consumer Code). The mediator's contact details are given on request at
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>. Failing agreement, the
				dispute will be brought before the competent courts.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>16. Contact</h2>
			<p>
				For any question or to report a problem:
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.legal {
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
		color: var(--gray-200);
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}
	.legal ul {
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.35rem;
	}
	.legal a {
		color: var(--accent-regular);
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}
	.legal a:hover,
	.legal a:focus {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}
	.updated {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-300);
	}
	.summary {
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-regular);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
	}
	.summary p {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	code {
		font-size: 0.9em;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
		padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
		border-radius: 0.25em;
	}
</style>
